BC textures that can be read back, as desktop OpenGL allows and OpenGL ES doesn't: a copy of every BC upload to a
2D texture, kept in a deleted file (a game's atlases are gigabytes), from which glGetCompressedTexImage,
GL_TEXTURE_COMPRESSED_IMAGE_SIZE and glGetTexImage (decoded, BC1-BC5) answer. Factorio checks its GPU texture
compressor that way at every start; without it, it aborts ("VideoBitmapOpenGL.cpp:267: data.size() ==
size_t(size) + offset").

